    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Sweet and sour: The Briefing for 23 March 2026</title>
      <link>https://globalcompetitionreview.com/article/sweet-and-sour-the-briefing-23-march-2026</link>
      <description>Turkey’s Competition Authority has launched a resale price maintenance probe into Haribo. Announced today, the investigation is also examining potentially unlawful exclusivity causes included in the sweet maker’s contracts with sellers. Also in The Briefing, the Dutch competition authority again delays its decision on Apple’s commission rates for dating app providers and China announces ongoing raids in the food delivery market.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://globalcompetitionreview.com/article/sweet-and-sour-the-briefing-23-march-2026</guid>
      <enclosure url="https://d2qu5xmcgmzxnb.cloudfront." length="0" type="image/jpeg"/>
